  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, be the circumcenter of a triangle with vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> denote the circumradius, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>β</mi></math> denote the area and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>γ</mi></math> denote the perimeter of the triangle. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></math> is"
  },
